ndom roll of this die?" 13194139535619 17592186045417 true] [17592186171848 1074 "Let $X$ represent the number the die lands on. From the problem statement, we know that $X \\sim U \\{1, 2, \\ldots, 12\\}$, and we wish to compute $\\textrm E[X]$.\n\nIn general, if $X \\sim U \\{a, a + 1, \\ldots, b\\}$, then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\dfrac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X \\sim U \\{1, 2, \\ldots, 12\\}$, we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\dfrac{1+12}{2} = 6.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected value is $6.5$." 13194139535619 17592186045417 false] [17592186171848 1074 "Let $X$ represent the number the die lands on. From the problem statement, we know that $X \\sim U \\{1, 2, \\ldots, 12\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\textrm E[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X \\sim U \\{a, a + 1, \\ldots, b\\},$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\dfrac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X \\sim U \\{ 1, 2, \\ldots, 12\\},$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\dfrac{1+12}{2} = 6.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected value is $6.5.$" 13194139535619 17592186045417 true] [17592186171849 1071 "A fair die has sides labeled with numbers $4$ through $15$. What is the variance of the numbers obtained when rolling this die?" 13194139535619 17592186045417 false] [17592186171849 1071 "A fair die has sides labeled with numbers $4$ through $15.$ What is the variance of the numbers obtained when rolling this die?" 13194139535619 17592186045417 true] [17592186171849 1074 "Let $X$ represent the number the die lands on. From the problem statement, we know that $X \\sim U \\{ 4, 5, \\ldots, 15 \\},$ and we wish to compute $\\textrm{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X \\sim U \\{a, a + 1, \\ldots, b\\},$ then the variance of $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\dfrac{|S|^2-1}{12}\n$$\n\nwhere $S = \\{a, a+1, \\ldots, b\\}.$\n\nNow, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|S| & =b-a+1 \\